  "adaptations": [
    "This native workspace follows the reference composition and white/teal/coral visual language but is not a pixel-exact copy of the concept image.",
    "The original inspector region exposes macros 5–8 so all eight native macros remain visible; route editing and the detailed inspector open through Edit routes.",
    "The concept's four envelope tabs and unrestricted scene Blend are not fabricated: the amplitude envelope is visible and the second native envelope and supported scene modes remain in the full editor.",
    "Oscillator and effect algorithms, labels, values, and enabled states come from the real processor; absent algorithm parameters are disabled, not fictional controls.",
    "Filter envelope amount replaces the image's independent per-filter drive. Surge's shared waveshaper drive remains in the full editor.",
    "Both filter responses share one plot; it is a labeled preview rather than a measurement of all nonlinear filter modes. The LFO is also a waveform preview.",
    "The analyzer uses real output levels and the native scope action; no fabricated spectrogram is painted into the skin.",
    "The first eight effect slots each expose their real algorithm and two dynamic parameters. All sixteen native slots and complete parameter sets remain in the full editor.",
    "The compact oscillator and effect controls follow the dense reference geometry. Keyboard focus, native names and value access are provided by the shared controls; the Accessible name is a design direction, not a certification claim.",
    "Shared header actions provide real preset navigation, scene selection, skin selection and full-editor access in place of decorative concept-only navigation."
  ]
}
